<title>FRANCE: Rouen May 1-14 grain exports at 272,121 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Rouen May 1-14 grain exports at 272,121 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exports from the French port of Rouen reached 272,121 tonnes between May 1 and May 14, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Grain exports were 174,000 tonnes for the whole of May 1996.</p>
<p>The May 1-14 grain total included 216,321 tonnes of wheat and 55,800 tonnes of barley.</p>
<p>Officials gave the following breakdown by destination (in tonnes).</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    West Africa		   37,800</p>
<p>    Algeria			 22,700</p>
<p>    Britain			  6,530</p>
<p>    Ireland			  1,650</p>
<p>    Italy			  121,941</p>
<p>    La Reunion		     3,000</p>
<p>    Turkey			  22,700</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    South Africa		  24,800</p>
<p>    Tunisia			 25,000</p>
<p>    Turkey			   6,000</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
